  "body": "When translating a valid C program that declares a local variable without using it, c2go preserves the unused variable in the generated Go code:\n```go\nvar c int32 = int32(0)\n```\nThis causes the generated Go program to fail during compilation, because Go does not allow unused local variables. It may be helpful for c2go to either omit such unused variables when safe, or emit a blank assignment such as `_ = c` to satisfy Go\u2019s unused-variable rule.\n**To Reproduce**\n```c\nint main(void) {\n    int c = 0;\n\n    return 0;\n}\n```\nThe generated Go code contains:\n```go\nfunc main() {\n        var c int32 = int32(0)\n        return\n}\n```\n**Observed Behavior**\n```\n# command-line-arguments\n./test.go:12:6: c declared and not used\n```\nThe generated Go code fails to compile because c is declared but never used.",
